  "market_context": "Price broke below the 200 MA and executed a near-90-degree steep impulse down, indicating strong bearish momentum. The retracement was shallow, halting precisely at the 0.382 Fib level which coincided with the 21 MA.",
  "key_observation": "The steepness of the impulse move (near 90-degree angle) caused price to retrace only to the 0.382 Fibonacci level, which aligned exactly with the 21-period moving average—creating high-probability confluence for a trend continuation short.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a steep downward impulse move breaking below the 200 MA, characterized as 'extremely bearish' with a near-90-degree angle.",
    "Step 2: Drew a Fibonacci retracement from the swing high (~1.36583) to the swing low (~1.35482) on the 15-minute chart.",
    "Step 3: Observed that the retracement halted precisely at the 0.382 Fib level, which converged with the 21-period moving average.",
    "Step 4: Noted the rejection off the 21 MA and 0.382 zone as confirmation of trend continuation, favoring a short entry targeting prior swing low and Fib extensions."
  ],
  "outcome": "Short trade taken at 0.382/21 MA confluence with stop above 0.618; price continued down sharply after rejection.",
  "lessons": "The steeper the impulse move (e.g., >45°), the shallower the retracement—often limited to 0.382. Confluence of Fib levels with dynamic SMMA (21 MA) significantly increases reliability of trend continuation entries.",
